# text = As many restless spirits , who have hunted fortune , fame , or pleasure through the world , retire in their decline to where they first drew breath , vainly seeking to be children once again before they die , so we , less fortunate than they in early life , but happier in its closing scenes , will set up our rest again among our boyish haunts , and going home with no hope realised , that had its growth in manhood -- carrying back nothing that we brought away , but our old yearnings to each other -- saving no fragment from the wreck of life , but that which first endeared it -- may be , indeed , but children as at first .
